-- title:
--   Generic-fibre character algebra: annihilator description and Hopf stability
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a commutative ring, $F$ a field which is an $O$-algebra, and $A$ a commutative Hopf $O$-algebra which is finite and free as an $O$-module and whose comultiplication is cocommutative; let $L$ be a field which is an $F$-algebra, and let $S$ be a submonoid of the convolution monoid `WithConv` on the set of $F$-algebra maps $F\otimes_O A\to L$. Write $\mathrm{ptSet}\,S$ for the set of those $\nu\colon F\otimes_O A\to_{\mathrm{alg}} L$ whose image in `WithConv` lies in $S$, $I_S\subseteq F\otimes_O A$ for the ideal of elements killed by every $\nu\in\mathrm{ptSet}\,S$, and $Q=(F\otimes_O A)/I_S$. Two hypotheses are imposed: separation, namely that an element $x\in Q\otimes_F Q$ is zero as soon as the algebra map $Q\otimes_F Q\to L$ induced by multiplying the values of $\nu$ and $\nu'$ kills $x$ for all $\nu,\nu'\in\mathrm{ptSet}\,S$; and antipode stability, namely that for each $\nu\in\mathrm{ptSet}\,S$ there is $\nu'\in\mathrm{ptSet}\,S$ whose underlying $F$-linear map is the antipode of $F\otimes_O A$ followed by $\nu$. Let $\beta=$ [`CartierDual.dualBaseChangeLin`](def/HopfAlgebra_CharacterClosure.html#L151) $\colon F\otimes_O A^{\vee}\to (F\otimes_O A)^{\vee}$ be the base change of functionals, $A^\vee$ being the Cartier dual [`CartierDual O A`](def/HopfAlgebra_CartierDual.html#L12) $=\operatorname{Hom}_O(A,O)$, and let $B_S$ be the $F$-subalgebra of $F\otimes_O A^{\vee}$ generated by $\{w:\beta(w)|_{I_S}=0\}$. The conclusion is threefold: first, $B_S$ coincides as a set with that generating set $\{w:\beta(w)(x)=0\ \text{for all }x\in I_S\}$; second, [`IsComulStable`](def/FiniteFlat_ClosureHopf.html#L232) holds for $B_S$, i.e. for every $g\in A^{\vee}$ with $1\otimes g\in B_S$ the image of the comultiplication $\Delta_O(g)\in A^\vee\otimes_O A^\vee$ under $a\otimes b\mapsto (1\otimes a)\otimes_F(1\otimes b)$ lies in the $F$-span of the elements $b\otimes_F b'$ with $b,b'\in B_S$; third, [`IsAntipodeStable`](def/FiniteFlat_ClosureHopf.html#L284) holds for $B_S$, i.e. for every such $g$ one has $1\otimes S_{A^\vee}(g)\in B_S$, where $S_{A^\vee}$ is the antipode of $A^\vee$ over $O$.
--
--   This identifies the character algebra attached on the Cartier dual side to a monoid of $L$-valued points of the generic fibre as the full annihilator of the vanishing ideal of those points, and records that it is stable under comultiplication and antipode, so that its flat closure in $A^{\vee}$ is an $O$-Hopf order; this is the dual formulation of Raynaud's schematic closure of the subgroup generated by a finite set of generic-fibre points. It is used in the analysis of reduction kernels of Galois representations of multiplicative type along admissible chains, and in the computations of character closures of points.
